; think_limiter_test.logo -- standalone test sidecar for the autoexec
; ThinkLimit budget limiter. One line of logic: run the limiter with a tiny
; budget and banner when the think close passes through. No RAG, no primer,
; no stream rewrite -- the ONLY thing under test is the limiter's SetOutputToken
; close (and, if the model tries it, the think-open suppression).
;
; Expected behavior (see README.md): the model thinks for about LIMIT
; tokens, the limiter replaces the next sentence boundary with the think
; close token, and the model writes its answer. The console shows the
; THINK LIMITER banner from autoexec and the close-observed banner below.

Make "currentToken" ThinkLimit :Piece 40        ; tiny budget so the limiter fires within the first sentences

IfElse (:currentToken = "</think>") [
  PrintBanner "THINK LIMITER TEST - think close passed (injected by the limiter or generated by the model)"
] []
